nic-Scheft</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Effects of experimentally-induced emotional states on frontal lobe cognitive task performance</article-title><source>Neuropsychologia</source><year>1999</year><volume>37</volume><fpage>677</fpage><lpage>683</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10390029</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0028-3932(98)00123-7</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Endler</surname><given-names>SN</given-names></name><name><surname>Kocovski</surname><given-names>LN</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>State and trait anxiety revisited</article-title><source>J Anxiety Disord</source><year>2001</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>231</fpage><lpage>245</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11442141</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0887-6185(01)00060-3</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Spielberger</surname><given-names>DC</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Spielberger DC</surname></name></person-group><article-title>Current trends in theory and research on anxiety</article-title><source>Anxiety Current Trends in Theory and Research</source><year>1972</year><volume>I</volume><publisher-name>London: Academic Press</publisher-name><fpage>3</fpage><lpage>19</lpage></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>